<title>USA: Medical Tech sets stock buy back.</title>
<headline>Medical Tech sets stock buy back.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medical Technology and Innovations Inc said Thursday its board has approved the buy-back of 100,000 shares in the open market over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>Chief Financial Officer Steve Gill said, &quot;It is managements' opinion that the stock is severely undervalued.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said directors also approved a resolution to buy back all shares from shareholders who own less than 100 shares. This represents about 11,000 shares from 480 shareholders.</p>
<p>Medical Technology now has 11.5 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
